From 1ee174ffc52039db167982bc22849d22f0f4cea8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 10:40:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10639/11362] The live-path eval now records the supervisor
 receipt (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6640)

No runnable path produced applied trajectory-supervisor receipts on the live
generator, which is why the refinement ledger never moved and why exp6844 and
exp6845 both report effect_eligible_score 0.

trajectory_supervisor_diagnostics() had three callers and not one could serve a live
applied run:

- scripts/arc_scored_path_lever_harness.py collects the receipt but is FROZEN
  pre-2026-07-28 and pins the retired Qwen3.5-9B-MTP. Its own guard refuses to start
  against the live Qwen3.8-27B pin, correctly, with the message that a run there
  measures the retired model while the prose claims the live path. It stopped me
  today.
- experiment_6776 collects the receipt but is hardcoded SUPERVISOR_MODE = "shadow",
  and a shadow receipt is explicitly not redirect evidence.
- experiment_6558 only reduces receipts others produce; it never replays a game.

Meanwhile arc_leaderboard_eval.py, arc_loop_solve.py, arc_sge_live_path_ab.py and
arc_action_provenance_worker.py all run the live path and call the diagnostics zero
times. So the 13.8-hour run that finished today returned two rows with the field
absent, both confirmed llm_reached true and both zero levels.

This adds supervisor_row_field() to the live-path eval and emits
"trajectory_supervisor" on every row. The shape is copied deliberately from the
lever harness, including its failure handling: a raising call becomes an error
marker rather than taking the row down, and a non-dict value becomes an error marker
too, because an absent field reads as zero to a flat consumer -- the ambiguity that
cost a full day of wrong A/B reporting on 2026-08-21.

6 tests, 3 of 3 mutations RED. One mutation removes the row wiring and leaves the
helper intact, because a helper nothing calls is precisely what this incident was:
the function existed for months while live rows carried nothing. The call-site
assertion is what catches that.

A supervised run on cd82 and r11l is now live under this change. Those two games are
chosen because they have demonstrated adapter-free level-ups, and a redirect is only
credited by a level-up -- the constraint identified from exp6681 and exp6844 earlier
today.

